{"name":"Blue Bobbin","hex":"#52b4ca","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"bobbin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spool or cylinder around which wire is coiled.","In a sewing machine, the small spool that holds the lower thread."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bobbin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bobbin","blocks":[{"text":"A bobbin or spool is a spindle or cylinder, with or without flanges, on which yarn, thread, wire, tape or film is wound. Bobbins are typically found in industrial textile machinery, as well as in sewing machines, fishing reels, tape measures, film rolls, cassette tapes, within electronic and electrical equipment, and for various other applications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Vintage_wooden_cylindrical_bobbin_.jpg/330px-Vintage_wooden_cylindrical_bobbin_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobbin","wikidata":"Q1520790"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Shuttle_with_bobbin.JPG/500px-Shuttle_with_bobbin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Shuttle_with_bobbin.JPG/1280px-Shuttle_with_bobbin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Shuttle_with_bobbin.JPG/500px-Shuttle_with_bobbin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vintage wooden bobbin, unflanged, wound with yarn and attached to a \"shuttle\" that fits it for use in a floor loom.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShuttle_with_bobbin.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ca_1900_bobbin_winder_by_Anders_Mattson_Mora_Sweden.jpg/500px-Ca_1900_bobbin_winder_by_Anders_Mattson_Mora_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ca_1900_bobbin_winder_by_Anders_Mattson_Mora_Sweden.jpg/1280px-Ca_1900_bobbin_winder_by_Anders_Mattson_Mora_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ca_1900_bobbin_winder_by_Anders_Mattson_Mora_Sweden.jpg/500px-Ca_1900_bobbin_winder_by_Anders_Mattson_Mora_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hand bobbin winder from c. 1900.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o